<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">ambush</ansi>

Travel encounters and camp raids may catch a company off guard. Your best
living, present observer uses Perception and their own light to spot it.
Dim light costs 10 points of detection chance; darkness costs 25. Concealed
ground costs another 10. Enemy stealth opposes your observer. Detection
chance is limited to 5-95 percent.

  Failed detection: the enemy gets the opening combat round.
  Ordinary detection: neither side loses its opening round.
  Detection by a margin of at least 30 points: your company gets the
    opening round instead.

The surprised side cannot attack, begin an automatic chant, advance an
existing chant, use an ability, or wind up in that round. Orders can be
queued. Passive defenses and guardians still work, and you can order a
retreat. Normal fighting resumes on the following combat round; world
time and ongoing effects keep moving normally.

Camp Watch keeps its usual chance to detect a raid and preserve your
rest. A successful watch also prevents enemy combat surprise. If the
watch misses, Perception may still prevent surprise, but does not save
the broken rest. A tracker who evades a travel ambush prevents the fight
altogether, as before.

The opening advantage is decided once for the encounter. Ordinary room
fights and random room encounters do not roll surprise (a random encounter
is a sudden appearance, and neither side loses its opening round), and
another company joining a group already fighting cannot give it a new
opening round.

See help battlefield, help travel, help camp, help retreat, and help
encounters.
